 HISTORY                                                          3032 1451
 -------                                                          3032 1451
 This evaluation was generated by Naval Nuclear Laboratory (Mar   3032 1451
 2023) [1] using the FLASSH code [2].  The physical model is      3032 1451
 based on a mixed elastic scattering treatment and includes       3032 1451
 coherent elastic scattering, incoherent elastic scattering and   3032 1451
 inelastic scattering components.  This evaluation is intended    3032 1451
 to be used with the companion 7Li(7LiH) TSL evaluation when      3032 1451
 modeling enriched 7LiH.                                          3032 1451
                                                                  3032 1451
 THEORY                                                           3032 1451
 ------                                                           3032 1451
 Lithium hydride (LiH) has a fluorite (NaCl) type face-centered   3032 1451
 cubic crystal structure with four Li and H atoms per unit call.  3032 1451
 The inelastic scattering cross sections were calculated in the   3032 1451
 incoherent approximations using the H partial phonon density of  3032 1451
 states from a VASP/PHONON calculation of 7LiH.  The LiH crystal  3032 1451
 structure and lattice constant from [3] were used in the         3032 1451
 VASP/PHONON calculation. The mixed elastic scattering treatment  3032 1451
 was used to account for both coherent and incoherent elastic     3032 1451
 scattering effects present in this material.  The coherent       3032 1451
 elastic scattering component was calculated in the cubic         3032 1451
 approximation using the FLASSH generalized coherent elastic      3032 1451
 scattering module using the 7LiH crystal structure and measured  3032 1451
 room temperature lattice parameter of 4.0831 Ang from [3] along  3032 1451
 with free atom coherent scattering cross sections of 0.439 b     3032 1451
 for H and 0.51 b for Li-7 from [4].  The incoherent elastic      3032 1451
 scattering component was calculated using the Debye-Waller       3032 1451
 factor derived from the H partial phonon density of states and   3032 1451
 an H free atom incoherent scattering cross section of 19.997 b.  3032 1451
 A H free atom total scattering scattering cross section of       3032 1451
 20.436 b was used to ensure consistency with the ENDF/B-VIII.1   3032 1451
 H evaluation. A phonon order of 500 was used to ensure both the  3032 1451
 inelastic scattering cross section and the S(alpha,beta)         3032 1451
 functions at elevated temperatures were adaquately converged.    3032 1451
